From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:57:10 -0400
Subject: libclamav: Bound OLE2 property traversal (#161)

Cache the reachable OLE2 directory-sector chain once and validate
property indexes against that chain. This prevents crafted directory
trees from restarting FAT traversal for every property and rejects
references beyond the reachable directory stream.

Check the scan deadline directly while building and walking the
property map so MaxScanTime is enforced independently of metadata
collection. Preserve traversal failures between the OLE2 enumeration
and extraction passes, and retain ownership of the extracted-name
store until it is safely returned to the caller.

Derive directory and allocation-table entry counts from the declared
sector size so valid 4,096-byte-sector files retain correct stream
traversal.

Reported by Ziyue Wang, Liyi Zhou, Strick, Maurice, and Chenchen Yu
of Disproof AI Lab, University of Sydney.

CLAM-3097

